<title>USA: Michigan's 1996 jobless rate lowest since 1969.</title>
<headline>Michigan's 1996 jobless rate lowest since 1969.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michigan posted an unemployment rate of 4.7 percent in 1996 -- the lowest annual rate since 1969, Gov. John Engler announced Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the lowest unemployment rate since man first walked on the moon,&quot; Engler said in a news release.</p>
<p>The annual jobless rate matched Michigan's 4.7 percent rate for December and November.</p>
<p>The governor also announced that total employment in his state climbed to 4.6 million in 1996 -- up 122,000 from 1995.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
